---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseStudyHeader from '../../components/notebook/CaseStudyHeader.astro';
import HeroReframe from '../../components/notebook/HeroReframe.astro';
import SectionRow from '../../components/notebook/SectionRow.astro';
import InsightLine from '../../components/notebook/InsightLine.astro';
import Fork from '../../components/notebook/Fork.astro';
import Versions from '../../components/notebook/Versions.astro';
import OutcomeStats from '../../components/notebook/OutcomeStats.astro';
import Reflection from '../../components/notebook/Reflection.astro';
import Tally from '../../components/notebook/Tally.astro';
import Annotate from '../../components/notebook/Annotate.astro';
---

<Base title="Biomotivate: Peace Platform -- VK">
  <div style="background: var(--paper); min-height: 100vh; color: var(--ink); padding-bottom: 120px">

    <CaseStudyHeader entryNum="02" />

    <HeroReframe
      original="Why are patients losing interest in VR therapy?"
      reframed="When does a tool built for everyone stop working for anyone?"
      entryNum="02"
      marginNote="Product intern. 4 months, summer 2025. VR, an addiction recovery house, and 20+ think-alouds."
      marginSub="(the reframe took six weeks. the answer was always in the usage data.)"
    />

    <!-- 01 brief -->
    <SectionRow num="01" label="the brief" pb="88px">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.62;margin:0 0 22px;font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 20,'wght' 400">
          I was hired to fix the UI of Peace &mdash; a VR video-therapy platform used at a residential addiction recovery house in Pittsburgh.
          Patients used it as part of their daily routine: they put on an Oculus headset and watched a short therapy video.
          The team was already tracking a steady attendance decline when I arrived.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.62;margin:0;font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 20,'wght' 400">
          The assignment was: clean up the interface. I found something else first.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="margin">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-hand);font-weight:300;color:var(--pencil);font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;transform:rotate(-1deg)">
          The UI ticket was real. So was the decline. I did both &mdash; folded the fixes into a rebuild I did myself in FlutterFlow.
        </div>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <!-- 02 listening -->
    <SectionRow num="02" label="listening" pb="40px">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.62;margin:0 0 22px;font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 20,'wght' 400">
          I ran
          <Annotate type="circle">20+ think-alouds</Annotate>
          and sat in on VR therapy sessions. Nobody struggled with the interface &mdash; long-time users navigated it without a second thought.
          What I noticed: they searched for videos they hadn&rsquo;t seen before.
          Almost everyone watched the one mandatory video and skipped the two optional ones.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:21px;line-height:1.62;margin:0;font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 20,'wght' 400">
          I tested one explanation first. If patients understood what VR therapy was doing for them &mdash; the actual science, in plain language &mdash; maybe they&rsquo;d be more motivated to show up.
          I designed educational flyers explaining the method and posted them around the house.
          [TODO: did attendance move after the flyers? confirm outcome before publishing.]
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="margin">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-hand);font-weight:300;color:var(--pencil);font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;transform:rotate(0.8deg)">
          Running the sessions gave me different data than the think-alouds. Sessions: how the content was used. Think-alouds: why.
        </div>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <!-- pull quote -->
    <section class="cs-row" style="padding-bottom:96px">
      <div></div>
      <figure style="margin:0;padding:24px 0">
        <blockquote style="margin:0;font-size:38px;line-height:1.22;font-style:italic;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-0.01em;border:none;padding:0;color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 40,'wght' 300">&ldquo;I know which ones I&rsquo;ve seen. I&rsquo;m looking for one I haven&rsquo;t.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="mono" style="margin-top:22px">Observed behavior &mdash; paraphrased across think-alouds</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <aside class="sw-note" style="padding-top:30px">
        <Tally count={4} />
        <div class="note" style="margin-top:6px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink-60)">4 of the first 6 participants searched for unseen content before watching.</div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 the turn -->
    <InsightLine
      num="03"
      label="the turn"
      validated="Long-term users declining as much as new ones"
      observed="Consistent searching behavior across 20+ sessions"
      assumed="Education alone wouldn't turn attendance around"
    >
      The interface was fine. The content had run out of people it was made for.
    </InsightLine>

    <!-- 04 the diagnosis -->
    <Fork
      num="04"
      label="the diagnosis"
      context="Attendance was falling among experienced users, not just newcomers. That meant it wasn't about learning the device. I had four explanations left."
      options={[
        { label: "Device friction. The VR headsets had a learning curve.", pathNotTaken: "Long-term users who used VR daily for other things were declining too. Ruled out early." },
        { label: "UI friction. The interface was confusing.", pathNotTaken: "No support tickets. Confused users usually file them. Ruled out." },
        { label: "Motivation. Patients didn't understand how the therapy was helping them.", pathNotTaken: "I tested this first with educational flyers. [TODO: confirm outcome before publishing.]" },
        { label: "Content. Stale and not personally meaningful.", chosen: true },
      ]}
      rationale="People searched for videos they hadn't seen yet. The ones who kept coming watched the same mandatory video every time. The optional extras were almost never touched. The decline included people who'd used the platform for over a year. That's not confusion or low motivation. That's running out of content worth watching."
      knew={[
        { text: "Long-term users declining as much as new ones. Observed in attendance records.", confidence: "observed" },
        { text: "Patients searched for unseen videos every session. Observed in think-alouds.", confidence: "observed" },
        { text: "Almost no optional videos watched. Observed in usage data.", confidence: "observed" },
        { text: "Flyers might still help as support material even if not the main cause. Assumed.", confidence: "assumed" },
      ]}
    />

    <!-- 05 what to build -->
    <Fork
      num="05"
      label="what to build"
      context="Once I knew content was the problem, the question was what kind of content would actually fix it. The team's first instinct was to add more topics."
      options={[
        { label: "More stock videos across a wider range of topics.", pathNotTaken: "More of the same, spread thinner. No reason any one of them would mean more to anyone." },
        { label: "Personalized videos generated from each patient's own input.", chosen: true },
      ]}
      rationale="Novelty wasn't what made the first personalized videos work. Early users rewatched them and asked to watch them again during free time. They came back to contribute more ideas. That's not novelty &mdash; that's ownership. More stock topics would still be content made for everyone. That's what had run out."
      knew={[
        { text: "First personalized videos were rewatched and requested again. Observed in pilot.", confidence: "validated" },
        { text: "One confound to name: patients felt they should watch because we made it for them. I saw this. It's real and it's a bias.", confidence: "observed" },
        { text: "Personalized production is slower and doesn't scale. Acceptable for pilot. Assumed.", confidence: "assumed" },
        { text: "More stock topics wouldn't create rewatch behavior. Assumed from past usage patterns.", confidence: "assumed" },
      ]}
    />

    <!-- pull quote 2 -->
    <section class="cs-row" style="padding-bottom:88px">
      <div></div>
      <figure style="margin:0;padding:24px 0">
        <blockquote style="margin:0;font-size:34px;line-height:1.3;font-style:italic;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-0.01em;border:none;padding:0;color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--font-serif);font-variation-settings:'opsz' 36,'wght' 300">&ldquo;I felt bad for not watching it. You made it for me.&rdquo;</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="mono" style="margin-top:22px">Patient, anonymized and paraphrased</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <aside class="sw-note" style="padding-top:30px">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-hand);font-weight:300;color:var(--pencil);font-size:17px;line-height:1.5">The hunch that started it all &mdash; and a confound I had to name. I&rsquo;m not sure how much of the engagement came from ownership and how much from guilt.</div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 the standard -->
    <Versions
      num="06"
      label="the standard"
      defaultIdx={3}
      versions={[
        {
          name: "v0",
          when: "first batch",
          text: "Generated the first videos with no constraints. Character inconsistency clip to clip. One tool's output sexualized a female patient's character and misrepresented her body type. No quality standard existed yet.",
          note: "We found out what we'd get by getting it. The failures were specific enough to know exactly what to prevent."
        },
        {
          name: "v1",
          when: "second batch",
          text: "Added manual review after each generation run. Caught problems batch by batch. No systematic way to prevent them before they happened.",
          note: "Better than nothing. Not a standard."
        },
        {
          name: "v2",
          when: "third batch",
          text: "Benchmarked available tools. Ruled out Veo and Sora: budget and latency. Chose Pika and Flikki with a fixed prompt template for character consistency. Same inputs, comparable outputs.",
          note: "Consistency became possible once the tool and template were locked."
        },
        {
          name: "v3",
          when: "shipped",
          text: "ChatGPT Projects with explicit guidelines and 'do not' instructions for every known failure type. Human reviewer on every image before it went to a patient. Character consistency maintained across the full story.",
          note: "The standard isn't just what to make. It's what not to make, written down."
        }
      ]}
    />

    <!-- 07 what happened -->
    <SectionRow num="07" label="what happened" pb="104px">
      <Fragment slot="main">
        <OutcomeStats stats={[
          { number: "+60%", label: "engagement (repeat views and voluntary sessions)" },
          { number: "+40%", label: "new patients who signed up for the first time" },
          { number: "[TODO]", label: "baseline and time window still needed before publishing" }
        ]} />
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="margin">
        <div style="transform:rotate(1deg);font-family:var(--font-hand);font-weight:300;color:var(--pencil);font-size:18px;line-height:1.5">
          Not a blind study. The same &ldquo;we made it for you&rdquo; effect that gave me the hunch could inflate engagement numbers. I&rsquo;m saying it here because it&rsquo;s true.
        </div>
      </Fragment>
    </SectionRow>

    <!-- 08 reflection -->
    <Reflection num="08" label="if again">
      I started something I knew I wouldn&rsquo;t finish. The personalized video system was too large for a 3-month internship. I started it anyway &mdash; so the team would have something worth finishing. I&rsquo;d do that again. What I&rsquo;d do differently: [TODO]
    </Reflection>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="cs-row" style="align-items:end;padding-top:40px">
      <div></div>
      <a href="/work/workbench-hr" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);display:block">
        <div class="mono" style="margin-bottom:10px">Next entry &rarr;</div>
        <div style="font-size:30px;line-height:1.2;font-family:var(--font-serif)">WorkBench HR: deciding what to build when you can build anything</div>
      </a>
      <p class="note sw-note" style="margin:0;font-size:16px;color:#66625A">p.s. This was written in a coffee shop on Forbes Ave, two blocks from where the sessions happened.</p>
    </footer>

  </div>
</Base>
